        "Brian J. Druker",
        "Nicholas B. Lydon",
        "Charles L. Sawyers"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BCR-ABL inhibition established a defining proof that molecularly targeted therapy can transform a lethal cancer.",
        "attribution": "Druker, Lydon, and Sawyers provide a coherent discovery-to-clinic account, though the underlying chromosome and kinase biology involved many contributors.",
        "maturity": "Durable clinical benefit and broad influence on oncology provide exceptional confirmation.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Whether the award should emphasize the therapeutic breakthrough or earlier identification of the molecular lesion is an attribution question."
        ]
      }
    },
